# Licensing

This repository uses a two-part license. Nothing here is "unlicensed" or
public-domain unless a file says so explicitly.

| Material | License | Applies to |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Code | [GPL-2.0-only](LICENSE-CODE) | `tools/`, `implementations/`, `src/`, `site/lib/`, `site/build.py`, `blob-matrix/`, and any other source file |
| Documentation and data | [CC BY-SA 4.0](LICENSE-DOCS) | `README.md`, `docs/`, `research/`, `upstream/`, `upstream-contribution/`, `workorders/`, `AGENTS.md`, `SCOPE.md`, `RENAME.md`, and CSV/JSON/JSONL data |

Full texts live in `LICENSE-CODE` and `LICENSE-DOCS`.

## Why this split

The clean-room components in `implementations/` were written against public
GPL kernel headers (see each component's clean-room statement). GPL-2.0-only is
the conservative choice for code derived from those sources. Research findings,
tables and prose are licensed separately so they can be quoted and reused with
attribution without pulling in code-license terms.

## Facts versus expression

Copyright covers the expression of a fact, not the fact itself. ISA identities,
container layouts, constants, hashes and other measured values are facts and may
be used freely; the *writeup*, code and datasets carry the licenses above.
Patents, trade secrets and third-party rights are not granted by either license.

## Third-party material

No proprietary firmware binary, decompiled output, or device-private data is
committed (see `SCOPE.md`). Public upstream sources referenced by the research
are licensed by their own authors and are **not** relicensed here. Synthetic
test fixtures are generated by committed scripts and contain no vendor bytes.

## Contributing

By contributing, you agree that your contribution is licensed under the same
terms as the material it modifies. See `CONTRIBUTING.md`.
